#
# STM32F746G Discovery board ext modules - for the external flash (/ext/bin), sent by upload-ext
#
# Everything the firmware (flash.dmd) does not need to bring /ext up: the drivers' configurations, units and rules
# of these modules go to /ext/cfg and are loaded once /ext is mounted.
#
dmuart driver=board/stm32f746g-disco/usart6.ini
# Hardware entropy source (/dev/rng); CLK48 comes from dmclk.
dmrng driver=board/stm32f746g-disco/rng.ini
# Civil RTC calendar; dmutc will supply UTC synchronization policy.
dmrtc driver=board/stm32f746g-disco/rtc.ini
rtc
#
# Network: eth0 on the on-board RMII PHY. dmnetif reports the interface as a
# "netif" device, networkd.rules and dhcp.rules then start networkd@eth0 (RX
# pump) and dhcp@eth0 (lease) for it. The pump brings eth0 up by itself once
# the PHY reports a link (dmnetbridge 1.2.4+), so DHCP needs no manual
# "ifconfig eth0 up".
#
dmeth driver=board/stm32f746g-disco/eth0.ini
dmnetbridge
dmnetif
dmarp
dmroute
dmip
dmicmp service=icmp.ini
ifconfig
ip
ping
networkd service=networkd@.ini
networkd rules=networkd.rules
dmudp
dhcpc service=dhcp@.ini
dhcpc rules=dhcp.rules
#
# Wi-Fi: wlan0 on an ESP32-C3 running ESP-Hosted (dmesphosted's coprocessor/
# firmware, wired to the Arduino header over SPI2 - see the README of
# dmesphosted's configs/board/stm32f746g-disco). dmesphosted's wifi.ini
# configures the pins, the dmspi bus (dmspi moves the frames by DMA, dmdma
# and dmheap must be up) and the device. dmnetif lists wlan0 only when the
# ESP answered - without one there is no wlan0 and networkd.rules / dhcp.rules
# start nothing for it; with one they start networkd@wlan0 and dhcp@wlan0 like
# for eth0. "wifi" is dmnet's tool (scan, connect, save a network).
#
# The networks to connect to by themselves are saved in the "wifi" vault of
# dmsecrets (wifi save SSID / wifi connect SSID -s): dmcrypto does the
# cryptography and, through its /dev/crypto node (crypto.ini), takes its random
# bytes from /dev/rng; the vault is opened with the key of the device secret
# (/dev/devkey, DMBOOT_DEVICE_SECRET), so nobody types a passphrase. wifid, a
# service libsystemd starts for every network interface (wifid.rules; it ends at
# once on one that is not Wi-Fi), connects wlan0 to the saved network in range
# with the strongest signal. The vault is a file: DMBOOT_DMSECRETS_PATH (by default
# /ext/secrets.vault on the external flash, or e.g. /mnt/<card>/secrets.vault) sets
# DMSECRETS_PATH - wifid waits for it to appear.
#
dmspi
dmspi_port
dmesphosted driver=board/stm32f746g-disco/wifi.ini
wifi
dmcrypto driver=board/stm32f746g-disco/crypto.ini
crypto
dmsecrets
secrets
wifid service=wifid@.ini
wifid rules=wifid.rules
#
# DNS: the dmdns resolver, brought up once for the whole system by the dns
# unit (type=library) - no per-interface rule. Name servers come from the
# DHCP lease (option 6): dmdhcp reports them through dmdns's
# dmdns_provide_servers DIF on every lookup. nslookup looks names up from
# the shell.
#
dmdns service=dns.ini
nslookup
#
# Time: dmntp, loaded at boot by the ntp unit (type=library), is one of
# dmutc's external UTC sources - dmutc sets the RTC from it after the start
# (again every minute until the network is up) and then once a day. The
# servers: the DHCP lease's (option 42), else pool.ntp.org/time.google.com.
#
dmntp service=ntp.ini
#
# Telnet: telnetd (dmtcp + dmtelnet) listens on TCP port 23; every connection
# becomes a tty node with its own console@ / dmell, like a UART does.
#
telnetd driver=telnetd.ini
#
# SD card: on-board microSD slot (CN3) on SDMMC1. dmdevfs creates the host
# node /dev/dmsdio0, the dmdevmon service (common flash.dmd) monitors the
# card detect pin and announces /dev/dmsdio0/0 when a card is inserted.
# The DMA2 controller (dma.ini) and CLK48 from dmclk must be up before it.
#
dmsdio driver=board/stm32f746g-disco/sdmmc1.ini
blkid
#
# SD card file systems: dmfatfs mounts FAT/exFAT, mkfatfs formats a card. (automount, which mounts the card, is in
# flash.dmd: see there.)
#
dmfatfs
mkfatfs
#
dmlcdtft driver=board/stm32f746g-disco/lcd.ini
#
# Touch panel of the LCD: FT5336 on I2C3. dmft5336's touch.ini configures
# the I2C3 pins, the dmi2c bus (/dev/dmi2cx/touch_i2c, its i2c_bus friend)
# and the panel (/dev/touch, polled: its INT pin shares EXTI13 with the
# microSD card detect) - dmi2c is only needed as a module here, its own
# i2c3.ini would configure the same controller a second time.
#
dmi2c
dmft5336 driver=board/stm32f746g-disco/touch.ini
#
# Audio: the WM8994 codec - stereo headphone output and the board's digital
# microphone - on SAI2 (PCM, dmsai) with I2C3 for its registers. The config
# joins the touch panel's I2C3 bus node (touch.ini above) instead of
# configuring I2C3 again, so both work at once. The nodes are /dev/wm8994
# (codec controls and stereo PCM) and /dev/dmsai1 (the raw SAI stream the codec
# drives); an application plays through /dev/wm8994 with the DMDRVI_IOCTL_AUDIO_*
# commands (dmdrvi 2.7). dmsai needs dmclk (SAI clock), dmdma (DMA2) and dmheap.
#
dmsai
dmwm8994 driver=board/stm32f746g-disco/codec-with-touch.ini
#
# The audio service: dmaudio.rules starts a dmaudio@<name> for every audio
# device dmdevfs reports - here /dev/wm8994 -, mixing what the applications
# play (libdmaudio) into it.
#
dmaudio service=dmaudio@.ini
dmaudio rules=dmaudio.rules
#
# The display service: dmview.rules starts a dmview@<name> for the LCD
# (/dev/dmlcdtft0), which shows what the applications claim for it - with
# the channel between an application and its view (0.10), which carhmi needs.
#
dmview
dmview service=dmview@.ini
dmview rules=dmview.rules
#
# The car HMI demo (carhmi) and what it needs - the image decoders, the MP3 decoder - are on the SD card, see
# sdcard.dmd: it is loaded from /mnt/<label>/bin once automount has mounted the card.
#
#
# Shell tools (the ones of tools.dmd are added to the list by DMBOOT_EXT_TOOLS): not needed to bring /ext up, so
# they are not in the firmware. They are found by name in /ext/bin.
#
rm
tree
printf
touch
which
mv
find
